0..74 Comment "//! A type calls a module\'s function through the module\'s name, as a value"
75..84 Comment "//! does."
85..88 Comment "//!"
89..165 Comment "//! A theory states its types as functions to `Type`, and a model calls them"
166..242 Comment "//! through the module that declares them. The printer writes such a type as"
243..307 Comment "//! that call. So the type must read back as the call it prints."
308..311 Comment "//!"
312..389 Comment "//! `Standard.same(Integer)` calls the function and decodes the code that the"
390..469 Comment "//! call returns. `Standard.after(Integer)(n)` applies the call\'s result to one"
470..545 Comment "//! more argument. A second list after a type family is not a call, and the"
546..570 Comment "//! lowering refuses it."
571..574 Comment "//!"
575..650 Comment "//! Limits: `Standard.unit()` runs a function of no input. A qualified link"
651..728 Comment "//! ends at a value name only before a list. So the empty list stands for the"
729..743 Comment "//! bare name."
744..747 Comment "//!"
748..819 Comment "//! - see: #5213 — a type reads a qualified call and a call of a call"
821..880 Comment "/// The types of a small theory, each a function to `Type`."
